yourself and paste the output)**\n```\npython -c \"import zipfile,re;z=zipfile.ZipFile(r'D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\\data\\c526d8d6-5987-4da9-b24c-83466fa172f3.xlsx');s=z.read('xl/sharedStrings.xml').decode('utf-8','replace');print(re.findall(r'<t[^>]*>(.*?)</t>',s,re.S));print(z.read('xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml').decode('utf-8','replace'))\"\n```\nor, if openpyxl is installed:\n```\npython -c \"import openpyxl;wb=openpyxl.load_workbook(r'D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\\data\\c526d8d6-5987-4da9-b24c-83466fa172f3.xlsx');[print([c.value for c in r]) for r in wb.active.iter_rows()]\"\n```\n\nNote on the underlying GAIA question this file belongs to (\"velocity … using the final equation … for Reaction 7\"): it needs the numeric `Reaction 7` row (substrate concentration plus the paper's constants), so no answer can be produced without the decoded sheet — I'm not guessing it."}
